464 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Bangladesh is developing county with a rapidly increasing population rate. In 2025, Bangladesh's population is estimated at 173.9 million, with an annual growth rate of approximately 1.22% \(Wikipedia contributors, 2025\). Along with that the GDP is also increasing with a great number according to the latest data, the nominal GDP for the same year is projected to be around $467.2 billion, resulting in a per capita GDP of roughly $2,593. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4 5]
>>
endobj
465 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 222 0 R
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
466 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This fast developing and metropolitan busy life one thing that is alarmlingly increasing is that the health diseases. To cure from these diseases this large and growing population, urbanisation and rising middle-class incomes are increasing healthcare spending and demand for chronic-disease medicines \(diabetes, hypertension, cardiovascular\).  People are dying every year for these diseases. which is shown in the figure aside.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6 7]
>>
endobj
467 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (According to a recent survey, a Diabetic \(Type 2\) patient need to spend around 2518 BDT/ Month. Along with till 2024, there are 13.9 million adult who has diabetes in our country \(International Diabetes Federation, 2025\) .  In addition, this monthly spending on the medicine for a patient of Cardiovascular issue goes up to 8,000 BDT per month just only on the medicine. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8 9]
>>
endobj
468 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (So, it is only a analysis of three diseases, there are around 250 plus diseases that people are overall dealing with. and in this fast moving, undisciplined life of the people will must depend on the medicine in their lifetime. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [10 11]
>>
endobj
