<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (As a Least Developed Country \(LDC\), Bangladesh has benefited from a waiver of the World Trade Organization's Trade-Related Aspects of Intellectual Property Rights \(TRIPS\) agreement. This has allowed companies to produce and export patented drugs at a lower cost an advantage that will be extended until 2033. We do export 30.3% of generic drug. According to 2024 export data, the top pharmaceutical variants exported from Bangladesh shows in the chart.)
