/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The current ratio peaks above 20 in 2023 and drops to 12.5 in 2024, which is still exceptionally liquid for a pharmaceutical company. The step-down is consistent with two things we already know from the company disclosures: strong cash outflows to shareholders and fresh investment. In FY24, Square announced a record cash dividend and outlined a Tk 500 crore expansion plan, which together can draw down cash and reduce current liabilities from a very low base, thereby compressing a very high current ratio back toward a more normal \(but still conservative\) level. The forecast gently lowers the ratio to 12 by 2029F, a reasonable working-capital normalization path if the firm continues to fund growth primarily from internal cash while maintaining healthy, but not idle, cash balances.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
