627 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Recent Events: In the fiscal year 2023-24, Square Pharmaceuticals PLC declared a record cash dividend of 110% to its shareholders, reflecting strong financial performance and confidence in future growth. The company approved a Tk 500 crore investment plan aimed at balancing, modernization, rehabilitation, expansion, and acquisition of new capital machinery to enhance production capacity. Despite challenges faced during the July-August period, including labor unrest and significant flooding, which caused the first-ever revenue decline for a quarter, the company managed to post a 12.89% net profit growth for the first half of the fiscal year 2024-25, supported by increased income from investments and associate companies. Square Pharma also saw a 22.4% year-on-year export growth in FY24, expanding its global footprint with increased demand for its products. The company continues to face operating cost pressures due to currency depreciation and rising raw material prices but maintains resilience through strategic investments in research and development, introducing 39 new products in FY24. Government policies, such as increased duties and taxes on pharmaceutical products, and market factors, including labor unrest and flooding, have influenced operational performance but have not deterred the company's long-term strategies. The company also launched health awareness campaigns like the diabetes awareness cycling campaign in November 2024 and achieved PIC/S certification for Penicillin formulation, signaling commitment to innovation and quality. Ongoing plans include strengthening the supply chain and further expansion despite a challenging business environment in Bangladesh.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
