/E (The table summarizes the key profitability and valuation metrics that determine the performance of the selected companies. The P/B ratio of Square is less than the industry average, which means investors are paying less for each unit of their stocks compared to peers. This indicates that the stock may be undervalued or lower expected returns on equity in the future. The return on assets \(ROA\) is more than double the industry average for Square Pharma, which means that they are highly efficient in utilizing assets to generate profits. This strong operational efficiency makes its low valuation \(P/E, P/B\) even more striking, suggesting undervaluation. Additionally, the return on equity \(ROE\) is higher than the industry average and most peers, implying that Square is delivering better returns to shareholders compared to most companies in the sector. )
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [4 5]
