741 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Bangladesh is nearing the graduation of least developed country \(LDC\) and the move is likely to change the regulatory framework as well as the trade environment in the pharmaceutical industry. Square Pharmaceuticals in the past has been quite flexible in terms of patent regimes, favourable trade access, and lenient licensing processes; the privileges could reduce after the graduation of the country. This means that these changes can increase the cost of launching new drugs, reduce competitive benefits in export and domestic markets and could slow down the launch of products, especially those of patented or high-value drugs.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
742 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (High Domestic Competition \(M2\))
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [23]
>>
