<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Since the classification of a Post-Least Developed Country \(Post-LDC\) was conducted, moral questioning of the pharmaceutical prices, the application of intellectual property rights, and the availability of necessary medicines is likely to exert greater pressure on the policymakers, civil society, and press. Square faces reputational risk in the event that the prices of patented drugs are set too high or too high to be accessible, particularly to low-income patients, and this fails to generate regulatory backlash or poor publicity.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [17]
